#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128911 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a453400-6363-5782-b346-aae37570c9bc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Complex Eigenvalues of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "3958f8c6-0808-510b-81f5-bb82de6a203f" :question/math-academy-id "e-5904" :question/problem "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I$:\n\n﻿﻿﻿$\\begin{bmatrix}1 - λ & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 - λ & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(1 - λ)(1 - λ) - 2(-2) &= 0 \\\\\n1 - 2λ + λ^{2} + 4 &= 0 \\\\\nλ^{2} - 2λ + 5 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-b ± \\sqrt{b^{2} - 4ac}}{2a} \\\\\n&= (- (-2) ± \\sqrt{(-2)^{2} - 4(1)(5)})/(2(1)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 ± \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 ± 4\\textrm{i}}{2} \\\\\n&= 1 ± 2\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are\n\n$$\n\\lambda=1\\pm 2\\textrm{i}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128912 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2eae4328-dd7c-5f77-8958-840cadb6f7f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Complex Eigenvalue of a 2x2 Matrix Given Another Eigenvalue"}] :question/id #uuid "2c47a76d-1b5d-5a10-a3c8-aff9647ca068" :question/math-academy-id "e-5905" :question/problem "Given that $\\lambda_1=-2+3\\textrm{i}$ and $\\lambda_2$ are eigenvalues of a real $2 \\times 2$ matrix $A$, find $2(\\lambda_1+\\lambda_2)$." :question/worked-solution "Since\n\n$$\n\\lambda_1=-2+3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nis a complex eigenvalue of $A$, the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of $\\lambda_1$.\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lambda_2=\\overline{\\lambda}_1=-2-3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(λ_{1} + λ_{2}) &= 2(-2 + 3\\textrm{i} + (-2 - 3\\textrm{i})) \\\\\n&= 2(-4) \\\\\n&=-8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
